    // - and gcd(m, m) = m.
    //
    // This is the classic Euclidean algorithm using repeated subtraction.
    // It strictly decreases the larger argument while preserving positivity.
    // When m == n, we return m as the GCD.

    // Use a tail-recursive helper function (or just loop) to avoid overflow or stack blow-up.
    // Rust's i32 / i64 is not named int by default, but assuming int is an integer type alias.
    // Here I will assume that int is an alias for i32, but just use int as asked.

